    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\frac{1}{12}$",
      "worked": "The (table section, die face) combinations that score 6 are $(1,6)$, $(2,3)$, $(3,2)$ and $(6,1)$.\n\nEach combination has probability $\\frac{1}{8}\\times\\frac{1}{6}$.\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}P(\\text{score }6)&=4\\times\\frac{1}{8}\\times\\frac{1}{6}\\\\P(\\text{score }6)&=\\frac{4}{48}\\\\P(\\text{score }6)&=\\frac{1}{12}\\end{aligned}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
